I can't help but note that you didn't say much about Carl's second point: 
that someone must actually be harrassed.  More on this below. 

Further, what would be at issue ultimately is whether a hostile 
environment really was created, not whether "someone feels . . . that 
someone is creating a hostile environment," though, in fairness, Paul 
notes that not all such complaints are necessarily justified.

