  The following column resulted in my dismissal from a UC Santa Cruz
student-run "gonzo" publication.  Since they didn't run it, I distributed
it independently.  I am now being charged with sexual harassment. A female
student read it and feels personally harassed.  Freedom of Speech is
dead.  Heil the New Dawn.

                                         -Smitty
                                      bjsvec@cats.ucsc.edu


   SMITTY ON A HILL:  "Where's The Women?"

     It's an age old question, asked by all men at one time or another,
 from the Fonz to Ted Kennedy.  Now, it's my turn.
     I can already tell you where the women aren't.  They're not at my
 house, that's for damn sure.  The women are not in my classes, bars, or
 room.  They're not at my local haunts: Ferrell's, Logo's, or Denny's.  
I've been all around this one horse town, and I know that it's not just 
me.  I've discussed the subject at length with my cohorts, and the answer
 remains a mystery, not unlike the career of Bob Saget  (Incidentally, my 
idea for a funny home video would involve masked men stuffing him in the 
trunk of a maroon Chevette and rolling it gently off a cliff ). 
 
     Ladies, where are you at?  We see you driving.  Where are you going?
  We see you talking to tall, blond, Aryan surfer types.  Why?  Basically,
 there are a lot of guys out here who are starting to lose faith in that
 whole Boy-Meets-Girl, Boy-Loses-Girl, Boy-Gets-Girl scenario.  We're 
starting to hit a Boy-Meets-Girl, Girl-Hates-Boy, Boy-Touches-Himself-
And-Wishes-It-Was-Her plateau, with occasional moments of Boy-Meets-Girl,
 Girl-Is-A-Psycho, Boy-Runs.

     Let's look at this rationally.  I know that the award-winning films
 Animal House, The Sure Thing, and Fraternity Vacation weren't
 documentaries, but,  come on, we're not even close.  UC Santa Cruz is 
like day care for tall people.  We're all so busy feeling victimized, 
practicing our sullen looks, and getting in touch with ourselves, that
 we've lost sight of life's simple pleasures, like a vibrant sunset, an 
ice cold beer, and breasts.  All is not lost, however, because I think 
I've come up with just the thing to get us back on track and barreling 
down that highway called "Fun".

     Welcome to the search for Miss Nude UCSC 1994!  The way I've got it
 figured, there are about twelve thousand students here, half of whom are
 probably women, a significantly smaller percent of whom will send in 
nude pictures of themselves in the spirit of good, clean fun.
     OK now kids, just get ahold of yourselves.  I can already imagine you
 out there, drafting petitions, planning rallies, and painting protest
signs.  This being Santa Cruz, you guys will probably march downtown and 
riot, waving signs that say, "We Hate Smitty!" and "Legalize Hemp!". 
 Let's face it, those hemp guys really love a parade.  But seriously now,
 this is college.  You are all paying thousands of dollars for a small
 piece of paper, and the kind of life experiences you don't want your 
kids to find out about.  So, live a little.
     Before anyone out there starts writing in about sexism, the trouble
 with patriarchal society, or what you learned in your "How To Kill Men"
 class, I want you to know that this is a cultural piece.  I'm trying to
 disprove the notion that our university is turning out a pack of weasels 
who wouldn't know a good time if it came over to their house, drank all 
their beer, punched out a hippie, and puked in their sink.  
     OK, so now you're thinking, "That's all well and good, Smitty, but
 what's in it for me?"  Well, the winner will receive dozens of prizes, 
in the form of a case of Pabst Blue Ribbon, as well as the respect and 
admiration of her peers.  The winner will also get a night on the town.
  Unfortunately, the town is Santa Cruz, but that's not my fault.  The 
evening will start with a culinary extravaganza at the College Eight 
Dining Hall.  Following the meal, she will be whisked away, in the 
comfort and luxury of a 1965 Plymouth Valiant, to the theater.  ( I'm 
leaning towards The Specialist, but that's negotiable.)  After the film,
 we'll adjourn to the Kiva Hot Tub Retreat for the talent portion of our
 competition.
     The winner of the Miss Nude UCSC 1994 Contest will be determined by
 a handpicked staff of judges, consisting of friends,  associates, and my
 Politics Teaching Assistant, Kevin ( I've just got to pass that class).
  My judges have heard that women occasionally disrobe, but have limited 
personal experience to that effect.  Therefore, they will be closely 
monitored during all phases of the competition to ensure that their 
demeanor reflects the maturity required of such a lofty post.  There 
will also be a runner-up Miss Nude UCSC, in case the winner engages in 
any activity which may disgrace her title, like reading City On A Hill.
     Entries must be submitted to Scott Smith, Oakes # 807, before the 
October 31st deadline.  All entries become the property of, well, me, and 
are assumed to be intended for publication, or room decoration.  ( For 
the extremely shy, yet wild-at-heart women, semi-nude, almost nude, and 
fairly close to nude pictures will be acceptable.)  The winner will be 
announced in an upcoming "SMITTY ON A HILL", so stay tuned.
     I've got a trunkload of prizes and a judging staff with time on their
hands; So, let's get to it.  My friends think I'm a hopeless romantic for
 believing anyone will enter my contest;  I'd like to prove them wrong.
  Besides, just think how "Miss Nude UCSC 1994" will stand out on a 
resume.


                               Peace,
                                 Smitty

